      "The economist Kate Raworth has offered a compelling visual compass for escaping this dead end through her framework of 'Doughnut Economics': human societies must navigate the safe and just space between an inner social foundation—ensuring that no human being falls short of food, healthcare, housing, education, and political voice—and an outer ecological ceiling beyond which climate destabilisation, ocean acidification, and chemical pollution trigger irreversible planetary collapse.",
