"INTERVIEWER: How, then, can post-industrial societies reconcile genuine flexibility and technological innovation with dignity and security for every worker?",
"PROFESSOR VANCE: By decoupling basic social protection from traditional single-employer contracts while re-regulating platform power: establishing a legal presumption of employee status for platform-controlled workers unless genuine independence is proven; creating universal, portable social rights—healthcare, paid leave, pensions, and lifelong training—that follow the person across every career transition; and strengthening sectoral collective bargaining so workers share fairly in the productivity gains of automation."
