"texte": [
"Mr President, Excellencies, Distinguished Finance Ministers, Ladies and Gentlemen, taxation is far more than a dry accounting mechanism for balancing public ledgers; it is the lifeblood of democratic citizenship and the tangible expression of social solidarity. Without fair, predictable public revenues, no state can fund universal schools, hospitals, clean energy grids, independent courts, or social insurance. Yet over the past four decades, the international tax architecture—originally designed in the 1920s for an era of physical factories and tangible goods—has been systematically outmanoeuvred by globalised multinational corporations and digital monopolies that book astronomical profits in zero-tax shell jurisdictions while relying upon public infrastructure, educated workforces, and consumer markets elsewhere.",
"As the economist Gabriel Zucman has documented in 'The Hidden Wealth of Nations', nearly forty percent of multinational corporate profits earned outside their home countries are artificially shifted into tax havens through intra-firm transfer pricing, royalty payments on intangible intellectual property, and fictional debt arrangements. This silent fiscal haemorrhage deprives governments worldwide—and developing nations in particular—of hundreds of billions of dollars annually, shifting the tax burden onto wage earners, small domestic businesses, and regressive consumption taxes.",
